{"c":[{"id":"cd4ef639b21c204f","sum":"Operator 2026-10-21: discoverable doctor commands (probe, smoke) never write; writes only via 'stockroom doctor fix <name>'. About five installs, nightly embed, rollout takes days; tune for a finished embed. A power loss may need the troubleshooting page, not an empty warehouse.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"ed5a4442c6ce5e9c","sum":"Doctor rule (operator, 2026-10-21): discoverable doctor commands (probe, smoke) never write; writes only via 'stockroom doctor fix <name>'. DuckDB 2.0.0 vss HNSW replay bug: auto-checkpoint folds the wal, index misses replayed rows; moot once index and vss were dropped.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261021T174235Z-774be06df86dea8f","text":"stockroom doctor rule (operator, 2026-10-21): any discoverable doctor command (probe, smoke) never writes. Every doctor write sits behind 'stockroom doctor fix <name>' and runs only when named. First fix planned: 'doctor fix hnsw-wal' for the DuckDB 2.0.0 HNSW replay bug.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261021T175900Z-bd6ed7dba4d68c72","text":"DuckDB 2.0.0 replay bug goes silent: other writers succeed, the wal grows, and past checkpoint_threshold (16 MiB) the auto-checkpoint folds it. Then the HNSW index silently lacks the replayed rows (pragma_hnsw_index_info count < count(*)); top-k skips them. A rebuild fixes it.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"3315768ae2a907e4","sum":"Operator 2026-10-21: about five installs, nightly embed, rollout takes days; tune for a finished embed. A power loss may need the troubleshooting page and must not empty the warehouse. The HNSW doctor-only fold check and 'doctor fix hnsw-rebuild' went with the dropped index.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261021T191821Z-1972e75cf1dd3323","text":"Operator 2026-10-21: silent HNSW fold is doctor-only, plus an index-coverage check. No repair on reconnect. The fix command is doctor fix hnsw-rebuild.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261021T193821Z-1b68223f17357c6b","text":"Operator 2026-10-21: about five installs, nightly embed, rollout is days. Tune for a finished embed. A power loss may need the troubleshooting page. It must not empty the warehouse. HNSW drops only around inserts.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"2f50c65a5d0f58b3","sum":"HNSW re-add (2026-10-21, 1.5.4, 2.0.0): index down until all embedding deletes run, then one recreate. Delete with index up leaks one at checkpoint/close (no-match does not); recreate between deletes leaks. No checkpoint while down. Drop, delete, recreate, checkpoint stays flat.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"594740d627151f97","sum":"HNSW, for any later re-add (2026-10-21, DuckDB 1.5.4 and 2.0.0): deleting embeddings rows with the index up leaks one index copy at checkpoint or process close; a no-match delete does not. Drop index, delete, recreate, checkpoint keeps used blocks flat.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261021T200533Z-dc75d974ecb1c63f","text":"2026-10-21: deleting embeddings rows with the HNSW index up leaks one index copy at checkpoint or process close, on DuckDB 1.5.4 and 2.0.0. A no-match delete does not. The drop covers those deletes, not only inserts.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261021T202433Z-25b36bcacf2f9117","text":"2026-10-21 eleventh L4 preflight PASS WITH ADVISORY. Drop, delete, recreate, checkpoint keeps HNSW used blocks flat on DuckDB 1.5.4 and 2.0.0. Advisories unadopted: checkpoint while the index is down; ingest keeps the index down for the whole process.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"a03e92dc6ad2d6f7","sum":"HNSW write rules, for any later re-add (operator 2026-10-21): keep the index down until every embedding delete in the process has run, then recreate once (a recreate between deletes leaks a copy); no checkpoint while it is down. Growth tests assert used blocks each cycle.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261021T211831Z-daa0544e233ebf48","text":"Growth test asserts used blocks or a high-water of one index over the start, every cycle. No checkpoint while the HNSW index is down; the next cycle reclaims that free copy. Operator 2026-10-21.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261021T213401Z-eb3da00d50779e55","text":"HNSW stays down until every embedding delete in the process has run, then one recreate. A recreate between two deletes leaks a used copy on DuckDB 1.5.4 and 2.0.0. Operator 2026-10-21.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
